      "notes": [
        "eunt with the complementary infinitive mirari expresses motion undertaken for a purpose: literally, 'people go to marvel at'.",
        "miror is a deponent verb. The infinitive mirari has passive morphology but active meaning: 'to marvel at' or 'to admire'.",
        "alta is a substantivized neuter plural adjective, literally 'the high things' or 'the heights', with montium as a dependent genitive.",
        "The accusative phrases alta montium, ingentes fluctus maris, latissimos lapsus fluminum, oceani ambitum, and gyros siderum are coordinated objects of mirari.",
        "latissimos is the superlative of latus. Here the superlative is naturally intensive as well as literal, emphasizing the immense breadth or extent of the rivers' courses.",
        "lapsus denotes movement, course, or flowing motion; with fluminum it refers to the courses or flowing expanses of rivers.",
        "ambitus denotes a going around, circuit, or encompassing sweep; oceani ambitum evokes the vast circuit or extent of the ocean.",
        "gyros, from Greek γῦρος, refers to circular movements or revolutions; gyros siderum therefore denotes the revolutions or circling motions of the heavenly bodies.",
        "se ipsos is an emphatic reflexive expression. se supplies the reflexive object of relinquunt, while ipsos intensifies it: 'their very selves'.",
        "The final et is rhetorically adversative in context: after enumerating the wonders people travel to contemplate, the sentence turns sharply to the paradox that they neglect or leave behind themselves."
      ]
